    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on September 7th hinges on capitalizing on favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.14) serves as our cornerstone play today; he benefits from a potent +14% platoon adjustment against Law, who struggles to neutralize his profile, and his #3 spot in the order maximizes his high-OBP output. **Trevor Story** (67.25) follows closely as our most efficient middle-infield option. His score is bolstered by a +12% SP skill rating against Rodriguez, who has been susceptible to power hitters of **Story**\u2019s profile recently. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** (63.28) is a lock in the outfield, primarily because he faces a pitcher in Gasser whose slow delivery creates an advantageous environment for **Suzuki** to potentially swipe a base, effectively addressing our ongoing need for speed.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who finished just shy of the 40.0 threshold at 39.94. While the park factors were favorable for a late-game surge, his negative platoon split and a tough matchup against the efficiency of Ryan ultimately relegated him to the bench to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, **Max Muncy** (43.60) and **Austin Riley** (41.94) are teetering near the floor of our starting criteria. Both are being suppressed by elite opposing SPs\u2014Cease and Luzardo, respectively\u2014and we are forced to weather the negative efficiency impact of their SP skill ratings simply because we lack superior replacements currently active.\n\nRisks remain present across the board, particularly with **James Wood** (50.12). Despite his elite 0.417 xwOBA, the head-to-head matchup against Pivetta\u2019s high-strikeout stuff creates a substantial volatility risk that keeps his score in the marginal range. We are also monitoring the status of **Corbin Carroll**, who remains unavailable; his absence is a significant blow to our SB production, forcing us to rely on the situational awareness of players like **Brice Turang**, who faces the veteran Boyd today. With **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Josh Naylor** unavailable due to injury and scheduling, respectively, the bottom of our lineup is playing a defensive game to keep our ratios stable while we wait for high-ceiling contributors like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Isaac Paredes**, or our developing prospects like **Dalton Rushing** and **Cole Young** to potentially rotate back into the mix.",
